   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "e445",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 10,
   "y": 5785.0,
   "width": 1357.0,
   "height": 100.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 2114689613,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1061266563,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Contiguous KV allocation suffers from external fragmentation because growing requests require contiguous physical memory.\nPagedAttention breaks KV into fixed-size blocks, so logical token sequences can map to scattered physical GPU blocks,\nmaking fragmented free memory reusable. The trade-off is bounded internal fragmentation in the partially filled final\nblock (waste < P). Prefix caching then addresses a separate problem: duplicated KV across requests sharing the same prefix.",
   "originalText": "Contiguous KV allocation suffers from external fragmentation because growing requests require contiguous physical memory.\nPagedAttention breaks KV into fixed-size blocks, so logical token sequences can map to scattered physical GPU blocks,\nmaking fragmented free memory reusable. The trade-off is bounded internal fragmentation in the partially filled final\nblock (waste < P). Prefix caching then addresses a separate problem: duplicated KV across requests sharing the same prefix.",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "e444",
